  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_PdfText">Use the extracted text as a help</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_PdfTextTip">If the PDF has a text layer, its text is put in the Markdown and sent to the VLM with the image (when the prompt has {pagetext}). Turn it off for a PDF whose text is not reliable (garbled characters).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_PdfHint">Turn on Step3 (reading the image) to get the most from a PDF</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_HiddenSheets">Include hidden sheets</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_HiddenSlides">Include hidden slides</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Recurse">Include sub-folders</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Fold">Kinds of file and conversion</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_FoldTip">Fold or open the kinds of file, the sub-folders, the engine, the DPI and so on. Folded, one line shows what is chosen. The steps are always shown.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Emphasis">Write bold and italic</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_EmphasisNote">(May be noise for other tools.)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Pictures">Save the pictures of the document</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_PicturesTip">The pictures pasted in a Word, PowerPoint or Excel file are saved in pictures/ (pictures/page-003-1.png: the first picture on page 3), and the Markdown refers to them where they are. PNG, JPEG and GIF are saved as they are; EMF, WMF, BMP and TIFF are turned into PNG. In Excel, a picture comes after the table or the text above the cell that it is fixed to.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Shapes">Cut out the shapes</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ShapesTip">The drawn shapes of a PowerPoint or Excel file (a group as one picture, and a shape of half an inch or more on each side) are cut out of the page image and saved in pictures/, like the pictures. A text box and a small arrow or line are not. Word is not supported. In Excel the place is worked out from the widths of the columns and the heights of the rows, so it can be a little off.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_EmphasisTip">Bold text in a line is written between ** and italic text between * (Word, PowerPoint, Excel). A paragraph (a cell) that is all in bold (italic), a heading and the title of a slide are not marked. When the Markdown goes to other tools, such as one that builds a knowledge graph, the ** and * marks can be noise.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_OffSlide">Include text outside the slide</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_OffSlideTip">PowerPoint: the text of the shapes that lie outside the slide (memos on the pasteboard) is written as a quote "Off-slide". They are not in the image of the slide.</sys:String>
