  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_Command">Command</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_CommandTip">The name of the program (in the PATH) or its full path. You install it yourself.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_Args">Arguments (one per line)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_ArgsTip">{input} = the input file, {output} = the Markdown file to write, {outdir} = a folder for the command. {input} is required, and {output} or {outdir} too (not when the output is read from the standard output).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_Output">How the Markdown comes</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_OutputFile">written to a file</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_OutputStdout">standard output</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_WorkingDirectory">Working folder</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_WorkingDirectoryTip">Empty: the command runs in the work folder of the document.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_Env">Environment variables</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_EnvTip">NAME=value on each line. A value is saved encrypted and shown as ********. To change a value, write the line again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_SendsExternally">This command sends the content of the documents outside the PC (it uses a cloud service)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_ConsentNotNeeded">Not needed (the command is treated as one that keeps documents on the PC).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_ConsentMissing">Not agreed yet. The command cannot be used until you agree.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_ConsentTitle">Sending documents outside</sys:String>
  <sys:String xml:space="preserve" x:Key="Ext_ConsentNotice">The extractor '{0}' sends the content of your documents (text, tables, images) to a service outside the PC.&#10;The terms of the service decide how it is handled. Usage charges may apply.&#10;Do not use it for confidential documents.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ext_NotFound">The command '{0}' was not found. Check that it is installed, and the PATH or the full path.</sys:String>
