  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_Excel">Sheet range</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelColumns">All columns on one page, as far as they stay readable</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelColumnsTip">Columns fit the width of a page and rows go on to more pages. A very wide sheet is still split, because it could not be read.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelSheet">Whole sheet on one page</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelSheetTip">The whole sheet goes on one page (one image) and is never split. A big sheet gets small text, so the DPI of the image is raised.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelPrintArea">Follow the print setup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Main_Cond_ExcelPrintAreaTip">Output as the print area and the page setup saved in the sheet say. Without a print area it is the whole sheet.</sys:String>
